/* ── the settings dialog on glass ─────────────────────────────────────────
   The panel already has one frosted surface and the operator is the one who
   asked for it: Appearance -> Transparent Acrylic Effect puts .advanced-visuals
   on the body, and every dropdown and popover marked .backdrop is then drawn
   through it. The settings dialog is the same kind of object -- laid over the
   screen you are working on, closed to get back to it -- so it is drawn the
   same way and with the same filter values rather than a second recipe of its
   own. One look, one place to change it.

   Only the section list is frosted, not the whole dialog. A backdrop filter is
   run again on every frame in which anything inside or under the frosted box
   changes, and the pane is a scroller: with the filter on the dialog, every
   frame of scrolling a category re-blurred all 1180x860 pixels of it, and so
   did every frame of any animation on the screen behind -- the dashboard has
   several that never stop. Measured in headless Chromium over the dashboard
   in dark, that held the dialog to about ten frames a second, scrolling or
   idle; with the filter on the list alone it stays near sixty. The radius was
   not the cost (24px and 100px measured the same), the area was, so the
   values are unchanged.

   The pane is drawn on the panel's own background, solid. Without a blur any
   translucency there is a second layer of text under the settings -- at 90%
   the dashboard's figures and headings could still be read through the form.

   The scrim behind it is lightened to match, and that is not decoration: a
   frosted sheet over an opaque black one is not frosted. What a dropdown has
   behind it is the screen, and having the screen back there is the whole point.

   The cards give up their fill. In this theme a card is already within one
   step of the pane it sits on -- measured rgb(16,17,19) on rgb(16,17,20) --
   so what draws a card is its border, not its colour, and leaving the fill in
   would have laid an opaque sheet over the glass for no gain. */
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal.pg-sm {
  background: transparent;
}
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-main {
  background-color: var(--pg-bg-body);
}

/* The dialogs a category opens over the settings are small and hold still,
   so they keep the whole sheet frosted. */
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-side,
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) #pg_settings_modal_extras .dialog {
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: brightness(1) saturate(1.5) blur(20px); backdrop-filter: brightness(1) saturate(1.5) blur(20px);
}
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) #pg_settings_modal_extras .dialog {
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-bg-body) 62%, transparent);
}

[data-bs-theme="dark"] .advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-side,
[data-bs-theme="dark"] .advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) #pg_settings_modal_extras .dialog {
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: brightness(0.7) saturate(1.7) blur(100px); backdrop-filter: brightness(0.7) saturate(1.7) blur(100px);
}

/* The surfaces inside keep their relationship to one another -- the list
   darker than the pane, the save bar darker again -- but they hold it in
   translucency now, or each would be an opaque patch on the glass. */
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-side {
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-bg-2) 55%, transparent);
}
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-foot {
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-bg-1) 55%, transparent);
}
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-link.is-active {
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-bg-body) 55%, transparent);
}
.advanced-visuals:not(.toolbar) .pg-settings-modal .pg-set-card > .card {
  background-color: transparent;
}

/* Only while the settings are open, and only then: the class is put on the
   body by the dialog itself. Every other modal in the panel still gets the
   scrim it was designed against. */
.advanced-visuals.pg-settings-open .dialog {
  --bs-dialog-backdrop-bg: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
}

/* A field held shut against autofill is not a disabled field and must not
   look like one: Bootstrap greys [readonly], and every field in the settings
   would come up grey until it was clicked. The mark is this software's own, so
   only the fields it shut are handed their colour back. */
.pg-set-card .form-control[data-pgro],
.pg-set-card textarea[data-pgro] {
  background-color: var(--pg-field-bg);
  opacity: 1;
}

/* The cell owns the row, the control owns the cell. Direct children only:
   inside an .input-group the control belongs to the group, and capping it
   there would pull the group apart -- so the group is capped instead. A
   form-adorn field needs no line of its own: its wrapper is the .form-control,
   the add-on inside its border, so the .form-control cap holds it whole. A
   cell whose control is wrapped in something else keeps the whole cell, which
   is the safe way to be wrong. */
.pg-set-card .pg-f-xs > .form-control,
.pg-set-card .pg-f-xs > :is(select.form-control),
.pg-set-card .pg-f-xs > .input-group { max-width: 11rem; }

.pg-set-card .pg-f-sm > .form-control,
.pg-set-card .pg-f-sm > :is(select.form-control),
.pg-set-card .pg-f-sm > .input-group { max-width: 19rem; }

.pg-set-card .pg-f-md > .form-control,
.pg-set-card .pg-f-md > :is(select.form-control),
.pg-set-card .pg-f-md > .input-group,
.pg-set-card .pg-f-md > .pg-pfield { max-width: 28rem; }

.pg-set-card .pg-f-lg > .form-control,
.pg-set-card .pg-f-lg > :is(select.form-control),
.pg-set-card .pg-f-lg > .input-group,
.pg-set-card .pg-f-lg > .pg-pfield { max-width: 34rem; }

/* A form-adorn add-on reads in the field's own type: the unit ("minutes",
   "days") is never larger than the number it follows, and the field is as
   tall as a plain one beside it. Value and unit meet on one baseline. */
.pg-set-card .form-adorn {
  align-items: baseline;
}
.pg-set-card .form-adorn > .form-adorn-text {
  font-size: inherit;
  line-height: inherit;
}

/* ── The hub ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Tiles of a fixed width, as many per row as fit, full width on a phone. The
   grid is the same idea as the dashboard's widget field: nothing is sized as a
   fraction of the window, so a wide screen gets more tiles rather than wider
   ones. */
.pg-hub-grid {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1rem;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
  align-items: start;
}

/* What each tile knows about its category, under the description: two or three
   label/value pairs read straight off the config row. */
.pg-tile-facts {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: .15rem .5rem;
  margin: 0 0 .75rem;
  font-size: .75rem;
}
.pg-tile-facts dt {
  color: var(--pg-fg-2);
  font-weight: 400;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.pg-tile-facts dd {
  margin: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-weight: 500;
}

/* The "/" hint in the hub search. A key cap, not a button: it says what the
   keyboard can do, it is not a thing to press with the pointer. */
.pg-hub-key {
  padding: .05rem .3rem;
  border: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-border-color);
  border-radius: .25rem;
  background: var(--pg-tint);
  color: var(--pg-fg-2);
  font-size: .7rem;
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.pg-hub-count { white-space: nowrap; }

/* ══ The settings modal ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Site Settings is not a place you go to any more: the button is in the
   header and the settings open over whatever screen the operator is on.

   The shape is a desktop settings window and it is the same shape at every
   width: the option list on the left, one pane beside it, and only the pane
   scrolls, so the list and the save bar never leave the screen. Three sizes:

     >= 992px   the dialog floats, the screen behind stays visible at the
                edges -- that is what says "this is on top of your work, and
                closing it puts you back" rather than "you have navigated".
     576-992px  the dialog takes the whole screen, the list narrows.
     < 576px    a phone has no room for both at once, so the list becomes a
                drawer over the pane. Still a list on the left, opened from
                the button in the dialog's header.

   Flexbox note that the whole thing rests on: a flex item does not shrink
   below its content on the MAIN axis unless it is told min-height/min-width 0.
   Every item in a column chain here therefore carries min-height: 0. Without
   it .pg-sm-main grows to the height of all its cards, the pane never becomes
   a scroller, and the save bar ends up a thousand pixels below the screen. */
.pg-settings-modal.dialog {
  --bs-dialog-width: min(1240px, calc(100vw - 6rem));
  --bs-dialog-backdrop-bg: var(--pg-scrim);
  --bs-dialog-backdrop-blur: 2px;
}
.pg-settings-modal.pg-sm {
  flex-direction: row;
  overflow: hidden;
  height: min(880px, calc(100vh - 3.5rem));
  border: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  border-radius: var(--pg-radius-sheet);
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--pg-surface-1), var(--pg-surface-2));
  box-shadow: var(--pg-shadow-sheet);
}

/* Viewport height on a phone is not a constant: the browser toolbar hides on
   scroll and 100vh keeps the taller figure, so a dialog sized in vh hangs
   below the screen with its save bar out of reach. dvh is the live figure.
   Declared after the vh rule, so a browser that does not know dvh keeps it. */
@supports (height: 100dvh) {
  .pg-settings-modal.pg-sm {
    height: min(880px, calc(100dvh - 3.5rem));
  }
}

/* ── the sidebar ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* The rail: 232 px on the menu's surface, its title, a 32 px search field,
   group names and 34 px items; the chosen item on the quiet fill with its
   icon in the accent. */
.pg-sm-side {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 232px;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: 232px;
  min-height: 0;
  padding: 18px 12px 0;
  border-right: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  background: var(--pg-surface-menu);
}
.pg-sm-side > .pg-sm-brand {
  margin: 2px 10px 14px;
}
.pg-sm-nav {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 0 0 1rem;
  scroll-padding-block: .5rem;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  scrollbar-width: thin;
}
.pg-sm-group {
  margin: 16px 10px 6px;
}
/* Every row looks the same whether it opens a pane or leaves for a page: the
   arrow on the right is what tells them apart. Colour is not used for that --
   in this panel colour already means something else.

   min-height is the touch target, not the text: 2.25rem here and 2.75rem in
   the drawer, where a finger is the only pointer. */
.pg-sm-link {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 34px;
  padding: 6px 10px;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 9px;
  background: none;
  color: var(--pg-fg-2);
  font-size: var(--pg-text-2);
  font-weight: var(--pg-weight-medium);
  line-height: 1.3;
  text-align: left;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.pg-sm-link i:first-child {
  flex: 0 0 1rem;
  font-size: 15px;
  text-align: center;
}
.pg-sm-link span {
  /* Wraps rather than ending in an ellipsis: at tablet width the list is
     12rem and a long category name was cut, with the full name shown
     nowhere (its tooltip holds the description). */
  min-width: 0;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
.pg-sm-link:hover,
.pg-sm-link:focus-visible {
  background: var(--pg-hover);
  color: var(--pg-fg-body);
}
.pg-sm-link.is-active {
  background: var(--pg-quiet);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  color: var(--pg-fg-body);
}
.pg-sm-link.is-active i:first-child {
  color: var(--pg-accent);
}
.pg-sm-out {
  margin-left: auto;
  color: var(--pg-fg-3);
  font-size: var(--pg-text-meta);
}
/* The search box over the list, and the hits that take the list's place. */
.pg-sm-search {
  position: relative;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.pg-sm-search > .bi {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 10px;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  color: var(--pg-fg-3);
  font-size: var(--pg-text-base);
  pointer-events: none;
}
.pg-sm-search .form-control {
  --bs-control-min-height: 32px;
  --bs-control-padding-y: 0;
  --bs-control-font-size: var(--pg-text-2);
  --bs-control-border-radius: 9px;
  --bs-control-bg: var(--pg-field-bg);
  --bs-control-border-color: var(--pg-field-line);
  --bs-control-box-shadow: var(--pg-field-shadow);
  padding-left: 32px;
}
.pg-sm-nav[hidden] {
  display: none;
}
.pg-sm-hit {
  align-items: flex-start;
}
.pg-sm-hit i:first-child {
  margin-top: .15rem;
}
.pg-sm-hit-text {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
}
.pg-sm-hit-text small {
  overflow: hidden;
  color: var(--pg-fg-3);
  font-size: var(--pg-text-meta);
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.pg-sm-hits-empty {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 12px 10px;
  color: var(--pg-fg-2);
  font-size: var(--pg-text-2);
}

/* ── the pane ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.pg-sm-main {
  display: flex;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  min-height: 0;
}
/* The pane's head as a dialog's: padding 20 16 0 24, the title and one
   line under it, the help and close icon buttons at the right. */
.pg-sm-head {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 4px;
  padding: 20px 16px 0 24px;
}
.pg-sm-heading {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
}
.pg-sm-desc {
  margin: 3px 0 0;
}
.pg-sm-head .pg-icon-button {
  margin-top: -4px;
}

/* The button that opens the drawer. Only a phone has it; on anything wider
   the list is already on screen and a button that opens what is open says
   something untrue. */
.pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-burger {
  display: none;
}

.pg-sm-body {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 6px 24px 20px;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  scrollbar-width: thin;
}
.pg-sm-notice:empty { display: none; }

/* The pane takes focus after it is replaced, so that a keyboard or a
   screen reader starts at the new content instead of at the body. That is
   programmatic focus and wants no ring. */
#pg_settings_modal_pane:focus { outline: 0; }

/* The foot under a body that scrolls: a line, padding 14 24, the buttons
   at the right ("Close" ghost, "Save" filled). */
.pg-sm-foot {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  padding: 14px 24px;
  padding-bottom: max(14px, env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
  border-top: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
}
.pg-sm-meta {
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* While a pane is on its way the pane says so rather than going blank, and
   the sidebar stays usable. The bar under the header is the only motion: a
   dimmed block with no sign of life reads as a screen that has stopped. */
.pg-sm-body.is-loading {
  opacity: .55;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.pg-sm-progress {
  position: relative;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  height: 2px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--pg-tint-strong);
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity .15s linear;
}
.pg-sm.is-busy .pg-sm-progress { opacity: 1; }
/* The closed dialog stays display:flex, so the bar loops only while busy. */
.pg-sm.is-busy .pg-sm-progress::after { animation-play-state: running; }
.pg-sm-progress::after {
  position: absolute;
  inset-block: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 40%;
  background: var(--pg-primary);
  content: "";
  animation: pg-sm-slide 1.1s ease-in-out infinite paused;
}
@keyframes pg-sm-slide {
  0%   { transform: translateX(-100%); }
  100% { transform: translateX(350%); }
}

/* ── the whole screen, below the sidebar breakpoint ────────────────────── */
@media (max-width: 1023.98px) {
  /* modal-fullscreen-lg-down asks for 100vw and the rule above caps it at
     calc(100vw - 3rem); the cap is what wins, and the screen behind shows
     along the edge of a dialog that is meant to be the whole screen. */
  .pg-settings-modal.pg-sm {
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  .pg-sm-side {
    flex-basis: 12rem;
    width: 12rem;
  }
  .pg-sm-side { padding-top: 14px; }
  .pg-sm-head { padding-top: 14px; }
}

/* ── the drawer, on a phone ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
  .pg-sm-side {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    inset-block: 0;
    left: 0;
    flex-basis: auto;
    width: min(17rem, 85%);
    border-right: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-border-color);
    /* Over the pane, the rail's translucent surface lies on the dialog's. */
    background: linear-gradient(var(--pg-surface-menu), var(--pg-surface-menu)), var(--pg-surface-1);
    box-shadow: var(--pg-shadow-lg);
    transform: translateX(-100%);
    transition: transform .18s ease-out, visibility 0s linear .18s;
    visibility: hidden;
  }
  .pg-sm.is-nav-open .pg-sm-side {
    transform: none;
    transition: transform .18s ease-out, visibility 0s linear 0s;
    visibility: visible;
  }
  /* Tapping beside the drawer closes it. Not display:none when shut: a
     pointer-events:none scrim can stay in the flow and needs no second rule. */
  .pg-sm-scrim {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 2;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .4);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity .18s linear;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .pg-sm.is-nav-open .pg-sm-scrim {
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
  .pg-settings-modal .pg-sm-burger { display: inline-grid; }
  .pg-sm-link { min-height: 2.75rem; }
  .pg-sm-head { padding-inline: 14px 8px; }
  .pg-sm-body,
  .pg-sm-foot { padding-inline: 14px; }
  /* Two lines of description on a phone is a third of the pane. */
  .pg-sm-desc { display: none; }
  /* The footer keeps only what has to be pressed. */
  .pg-sm-meta { display: none; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .pg-sm-side,
  .pg-sm-scrim,
  .pg-sm-progress { transition: none; }
  .pg-sm-progress::after { animation: none; }
}

/* ── a card's drawer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   A panel of the dialog (includes/settings/drawer.php), not a second dialog:
   it slides in from the dialog's right edge over the pane, which keeps its
   values under it. The dialog is fixed in the top layer, so it is the box the
   drawer is placed in, and its overflow clips the drawer while it is out.
   Visibility is not timed on the way in, so the focus can land at once. */
.pg-sm-drawer {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 5;
  inset-block: 0;
  right: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: min(42rem, 100%);
  min-height: 0;
  border-left: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-border-color);
  background: var(--pg-bg-body);
  box-shadow: var(--pg-shadow-lg);
  transform: translateX(100%);
  transition: transform .2s ease-out, visibility 0s linear .2s;
  visibility: hidden;
}
.pg-sm-drawer.is-open {
  transform: none;
  transition: transform .2s ease-out, visibility 0s linear 0s;
  visibility: visible;
}
.pg-sm-drawer:focus { outline: 0; }
.pg-sm-drawer-head {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: .75rem;
  padding: 1rem 1.25rem .75rem;
  border-bottom: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
}
.pg-sm-drawer-title {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.125rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
/* Scrolls on its own; a long command wraps or scrolls inside its field. */
.pg-sm-drawer-body {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  min-height: 0;
  padding: 1.25rem;
  overflow-y: auto;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
/* A band under a drawer's head that does not scroll: its tabs as the
   segmented control. */
.pg-sm-drawer-bar {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  padding: .75rem 1.25rem;
  border-bottom: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
}
/* A drawer's own buttons (Save, Try, Delete): a foot under the scrolling
   body, always in view. */
.pg-sm-drawer-foot {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  padding: .75rem 1.25rem;
  border-top: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  background: var(--pg-bg-body);
}
.pg-set-drawer-foot {
  justify-content: flex-start;
}
/* Tapping beside the drawer closes it; the pane shows dimmed through. */
.pg-sm-dscrim {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 4;
  inset: 0;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, #000 30%, transparent);
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity .2s linear;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.pg-sm.is-drawer-open .pg-sm-dscrim {
  opacity: 1;
  pointer-events: auto;
}
/* "Saved" after a save (confirmSave() in backend.src.js): one toast just
   under the head of the pane, or of the open drawer; the script sets its top
   from the head. Above the drawer and its scrim; only the toast takes clicks. */
.pg-sm-saved {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 6;
  top: 5rem;
  right: 0;
  left: 0;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  padding-inline: 1rem;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.pg-sm-saved > .toast {
  max-width: 100%;
  box-shadow: var(--pg-shadow-lg);
  pointer-events: auto;
}
.pg-sm.is-drawer-open .pg-sm-saved {
  left: auto;
  width: min(42rem, 100%);
}
@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
  .pg-sm-drawer { width: 100%; }
  .pg-sm-drawer-head { padding-inline: .875rem; }
  .pg-sm-drawer-body { padding: 1rem .875rem; }
  .pg-sm-drawer-bar { padding-inline: .875rem; }
  .pg-sm-drawer-foot { padding-inline: .875rem; }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .pg-sm-drawer,
  .pg-sm-dscrim { transition: none; }
}
/* The same content in Bootstrap's drawer on the page path
   (settings_maintenance.php and the like, with no settings dialog around it). */
.pg-set-drawer { --pg-drawer-width: min(42rem, 100vw); }
/* A long ticked list of a settings row (Ecommerce › Product feeds, the groups
   left out): it scrolls inside its own box under the filter. */
.pg-commerce-ticks {
  max-height: 18rem;
  overflow-y: auto;
}
/* Folded rows of a settings pane (includes/settings/fold.php; Assistants and
   agents): one framed list, a row a part, its head a button with the icon
   tile, the name over one line of state, the pill and a chevron. The card a
   row holds is drawn by its own function: inside the row it loses its frame
   and its heading, which the head already says; a heading holding a button
   (Add an agent) keeps the button. */
.pg-set-fold {
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  border-radius: var(--pg-radius-card);
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--pg-surface-1), var(--pg-surface-2));
}
.pg-set-fold-item + .pg-set-fold-item {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
}
.pg-set-fold-item.is-open {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-accent) 3%, transparent);
}
.pg-set-fold-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 13px;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 11px 16px;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: inherit;
  text-align: start;
}
.pg-set-fold-head:hover {
  background: var(--pg-hover);
}
.pg-set-fold-head:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--pg-accent);
  outline-offset: -2px;
}
.pg-set-fold-text {
  display: flex;
  flex: 1;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
}
.pg-set-fold-name {
  font-size: var(--pg-text-base);
  font-weight: var(--pg-weight-strong);
}
.pg-set-fold-line {
  overflow: hidden;
  color: var(--pg-fg-2);
  font-size: var(--pg-text-2);
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.pg-set-fold-chevron {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--pg-fg-3);
  transition: transform .15s ease;
}
.pg-set-fold-item.is-open .pg-set-fold-chevron {
  transform: rotate(180deg);
}
.pg-set-fold-body {
  padding: 2px 16px 18px 63px;
}
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card {
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
  background: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card > .card-header,
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card > .card-body {
  padding-inline: 0;
}
/* A settings card's body is an inner card (.pg-card-inner) with an inset
   line drawn by its shadow; inside a row that line would sit flush against
   the fields, whose side padding is gone, so the frame goes with it. */
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card > .card-body {
  border-radius: 0;
  background: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card > .card-header:not(:has(button, a)) {
  display: none;
}
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card > .card-header > :not(button, a, form) {
  display: none;
}
.pg-set-fold-body > .pg-set-card > .card > .card-header:has(button, a) {
  justify-content: flex-end;
  padding-block: 0;
}
/* Mailboxes' rules and blocked senders: the row's head names the part, so
   their own heading and top margin go inside a row. */
.pg-set-fold-body > .ws-mail-rules,
.pg-set-fold-body > .ws-mail-blocks {
  margin-top: 0 !important;
}
.pg-set-fold-body > .ws-mail-rules > .pg-title-section,
.pg-set-fold-body > .ws-mail-blocks > .pg-title-section {
  display: none;
}
@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
  .pg-set-fold-body { padding-inline: 12px; }
  /* A mailbox's row has two buttons (Test connection, Edit): beside the
     name on a phone they cut it to a letter, so they take a line under the
     pill. */
  .ws-mail-box-row > .ws-agset-edit {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    grid-row: auto;
  }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .pg-set-fold-chevron { transition: none; }
}
/* The ERP lists' quick look (includes/erp/drawer.php): 560 px wide, its
   tables straight under their section title. */
.pg-erp-drawer { --pg-drawer-width: min(560px, 100vw); }
.pg-erp-drawer table.table { margin-top: 0; }

/* ── Dashboard sales map (widget 1) ─────────────────────────────────────────
   The left panel of a two-track card: a period head and the outlines, with the
   period and map switches in a menu in the corner of them. The right panel is a
   plain .pg-list and needs nothing of its own. */
/* No overflow of its own, deliberately. .pg-split already gives this half
   `overflow-y: auto` once the card is wide enough to lay its halves out as a
   row, which is the only place a scrollbar belongs. Setting one here as well
   changed nothing there and broke the stacked card: any overflow other than
   visible cancels a flex item's automatic minimum size, so the panel was free
   to be squeezed to nothing -- measured at 0px, with the region list drawn
   straight over the map. */
.pg-smap-main {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
.pg-smap-main > .pg-head { flex: 0 0 auto; }

/* Three facts on one line in a panel half a card wide: let the line break
   between them rather than inside them, or "Tüm zamanlar" ends up split over
   two lines with "Tüm" alone on the first. */
.pg-smap-main .pg-head-line { flex-wrap: wrap; }
.pg-smap-main .pg-head-unit,
.pg-smap-main .pg-head-total { white-space: nowrap; }

.pg-smap-canvas {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  /* A floor, not a height. On a wide card the panel is a row and this box takes
     the space the head and the switch leave; stacked on a narrow one the panel
     is a column whose height comes from its contents, and an SVG that sizes
     itself from its box collapses the box to nothing. Measured at 8px before
     this line existed. */
  min-height: 7.5rem;
  padding: 4px 10px;
}
/* Both dimensions given, so the outlines fill whatever box they are handed and
   the viewBox does the fitting. Sizing from the width instead lets the drawing
   overflow a short row. */
.pg-smap-canvas svg {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

/* Every province starts as the card's own quiet surface, so the ones that sold
   something are the only thing with colour in the panel. */
.pg-smap-canvas path {
  fill: var(--pg-bg-2);
  stroke: var(--pg-bg-body);
  stroke-width: 1;
  /* The outlines are drawn at whatever size the card gives them, and a hairline
     that scales with the viewBox turns into a smear on a wide card. */
  vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
}

/* Four steps of the card's own accent, by quantile rather than by value - see
   pg_sales_map_steps(). Mixed towards transparent rather than written out as
   four hex values, so the ramp follows the card whatever colour it is given and
   holds in both themes. */
.pg-smap-canvas path.pg-smap-s1 { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-accent, var(--pg-primary)) 28%, transparent); }
.pg-smap-canvas path.pg-smap-s2 { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-accent, var(--pg-primary)) 48%, transparent); }
.pg-smap-canvas path.pg-smap-s3 { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-accent, var(--pg-primary)) 72%, transparent); }
.pg-smap-canvas path.pg-smap-s4 { fill: var(--pg-accent, var(--pg-primary)); }

/* Only a place that sold something is a link, so only that one takes the
   pointer. The rest still answer the tooltip, which is how "nothing here"
   gets said.

   .is-static is the card drawn for somebody who may read the report but not
   open the orders screen: the shapes still carry their figures, they just do
   not pretend to lead anywhere. */
.pg-smap-canvas:not(.is-static) path:not(.pg-smap-s0) { cursor: pointer; }
.pg-smap-canvas path:not(.pg-smap-s0):hover {
  stroke: var(--pg-fg-body);
  stroke-width: 1.5;
}

.pg-smap-tip {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  z-index: 3;
  display: none;
  max-width: 14rem;
  padding: .4rem .55rem;
  border: var(--pg-border-width) solid var(--pg-rule-strong);
  border-radius: var(--pg-radius);
  background: var(--pg-bg-body);
  box-shadow: 0 .5rem 1rem rgba(0, 0, 0, .15);
  font-size: 0.6875rem;
  line-height: 1.35;
  /* It follows the pointer, so it must never be under it. */
  pointer-events: none;
}
.pg-smap-tip.is-on { display: block; }
.pg-smap-tip b {
  display: block;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
}
.pg-smap-tip span { display: block; }

/* Tighter than .btn-sm, and never wrapping. Three period labels across a panel
   half the width of the card broke each one over two lines, which pushed the
   panel past the card body and left the half with a scrollbar of its own. */
/* The switches, as one icon in the corner of the map.
   
   They were a strip of buttons under it, and that strip cost the map a band of
   its own height in a panel that has none to spare. Worse, a .btn-group
   stretched across the panel gives every button an equal share of it whatever
   its label says, so three period labels wrapped to two lines apiece and pushed
   the panel past the card body. The head beside the revenue names the period on
   show, so nothing is lost by folding them away. */
.pg-smap-menu {
  position: absolute;
  top: 2px;
  right: 4px;
  z-index: 4;
}
.pg-smap-menu-btn {
  padding: .1rem .3rem;
  line-height: 1;
  /* Over the outlines, so it carries enough of the card under it to stay
     legible wherever the map happens to be dark. */
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pg-bg-body) 72%, transparent);
}
.pg-smap-menu .menu {
  --bs-menu-font-size: 0.75rem;
  --bs-menu-item-padding-y: .25rem;
  --bs-menu-min-width: 9rem;
}
.pg-smap-menu .menu-item {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: .4rem;
}
/* The tick is the only thing that marks the current choice: a menu row painted
   in the accent reads as a state, and these rows are a choice. */
.pg-smap-menu .menu-item.active {
  background: transparent;
  color: inherit;
  font-weight: 600;
}
.pg-smap-menu .menu-item:not(.active) .pg-smap-tick { visibility: hidden; }

/* One layer per view, both in the same box: the one not being shown carries
   .d-none rather than being thrown away, so switching back does not go to the
   network again. */
.pg-smap-layer {
  display: flex;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  min-height: 0;
}

/* ── Counter sale (add_order.php) ─────────────────────────────────────────
   One screen, two views. #pg_sale[data-mode] is "kasa" (till: prices with
   VAT, the change, large controls) or "belge" (document: VAT breakdown, the
   account and the due date). The server prints both figures in every row
   and the view hides the other set, so switching needs no request. */
.pg-sale[data-mode="kasa"] .pg-belge,
.pg-sale[data-mode="kasa"] .pg-belge-inline,
.pg-sale[data-mode="kasa"] .pg-belge-block,
.pg-sale[data-mode="belge"] .pg-kasa,
.pg-sale[data-mode="belge"] .pg-kasa-inline {
  display: none !important;
}
.pg-sale .card-header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: .75rem;
}
/* A card title of the sale screen: the look's section title in the form
   column, its status title beside it (pg-title-section, pg-title-status). */
.pg-sale-ch {
  margin: 0;
}
.pg-sale kbd,
.pg-sale-keys kbd {
  font-size: .7em;
  padding: .1em .4em;
  border-radius: 4px;
  border: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  background: var(--pg-bg-1);
  color: var(--pg-fg-2);
  white-space: nowrap;
  box-shadow: none;
}
/* A switched-off ghost button stays borderless; Bootstrap's disabled state
   would draw the outline the ghost recipe exists to leave out. */
.pg-sale .btn-text.theme-secondary:disabled { border-color: transparent; }
/* The view switch (till / document): one frame round both, the chosen
   view filled - a segmented control, as in the approved preview, rather
   than the joined .btn-group of the toolbar recipe. */
.pg-sale-switch {
  display: inline-flex;
  gap: 2px;
  padding: 2px;
  border: 1px solid var(--pg-border-color-translucent);
  border-radius: var(--pg-radius-lg);
}
.pg-sale-switch .btn {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: .35rem;
  padding: .2rem .6rem;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: var(--pg-radius);
}
.pg-sale-switch .btn.active,
.pg-sale-switch .btn[aria-pressed="true"] {
  background: var(--pg-bg-2);
  color: var(--pg-fg-body);
}
@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
  .pg-sale .pg-sale-lbl { display: none; }
}

/* Entry card: the product box and the customer box, side by side once the
   card is wide enough - measured on the card, since the column is. */
.pg-sale-entry { container-type: inline-size; }
.pg-sale-entry .card-body {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
}
@container (min-width: 620px) {
  .pg-sale-entry .card-body { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.75fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .pg-sale[data-mode="belge"] .pg-sale-entry .card-body { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }
}
.pg-sale-field { position: relative; min-width: 0; }

/* The product box: icon, text, quantity for the next product, Add. A
   .form-control wrapper so it wears the panel's own border and focus. */
.pg-sale-ig {
  display: flex;
  align-items: stretch;
  padding: 0;
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.pg-sale-ig:focus-within {
